{"meta":{"ph":"ˈstætʃuː; NAmE ˈstætʃuː","pos":"noun","stars":"★★"},"defs":[{"def":"a figure of a person or an animal in stone, metal, etc., usually the same size as in real life or larger 雕塑，雕像，塑像（大小通常等于或大于真人或实物）","ex":[{"s":"A statue commemorating Shakespeare and Tang was put up at Shakespeare’s Birthplace Garden in 2017.","src":"2024新高考II卷·语法填空","cat":"gaokao","year":2024,"t":"2017年，一座纪念莎士比亚和汤显祖的雕像在莎士比亚出生地花园落成。"},{"s":"Vinnie confirmed her ability to make a full-length statue by highlighting ______. （    ）","src":"2020天津6月卷·阅读理解B","cat":"gaokao","year":2020,"t":"温妮通过强调______证实了她制作全身雕像的能力。（    ）"},{"s":"Scholars have seen this idea in practice with ancient Greek and Roman statues.","src":"2020北京卷·阅读理解C","cat":"gaokao","year":2020,"t":"学者在古希腊和罗马雕像的实践中看到了这一理念。"},{"s":"Statues The statues include elements from 4______________________.","src":"外研社B7 U3","cat":"waiyan","t":"雕像中包含来自4                      的元素."},{"s":"For example, the mysterious large-eyed, bronze statues of the ancient Shu Kingdom, discovered at the Chinese archeological site at Sanxingdui, were believed to have been able to look across great distances into the stars.","src":"外研社B7 U6","cat":"waiyan","t":"例如,在三兴都井的中国考古遗址上发现的神秘的大眼青铜雕像,被认为能够横跨遥远的视星等."},{"s":"It was believed that the huge eyes of the large-eyed bronze statues from the Chinese archeological site at Sanxingdui were able to 2 ______________.","src":"外研社B7 U6","cat":"waiyan","t":"据信,来自三兴都井中国考古遗址的大眼青铜雕像的庞大眼睛能够达到2 ."},{"s":"Dozens of cultural relics have been found within the city, including city walls, two sacrificial pits, building foundations, jade ware pits and a burial area, as well as several thousand fine artefacts such as bronze statues and masks.","src":"外研社B7 U6","cat":"waiyan","t":"城内出土了数十件文物,包括城墙,两座祭坑,建筑地基,玉器坑和墓葬区,还有青铜雕像和口罩等数千件精美文物."},{"s":"It’s amazing that there are more than 8,000 statues, and no one in modern times knew about them until the 1970s.","src":"人教B1 U2","cat":"renjiao","t":"超过8000尊雕像,"}]}]}